			"notes": "# Project Flint v0.30.3-b → v0.31.11-a-test1\n\nThis update massively expands the end of the Wood Age and begins pushing Project Flint into more advanced construction, food processing, research, and early infrastructure.\n\n## Major Progression Additions\n\n### Sanding Station\n\nA new **Sanding Station** has been added as an important late-Wood-Age workstation.\n\n* Uses **Sand Paper** as a stored durability/resource.\n* Sand Paper provides multiple sanding operations before needing to be replaced.\n* Stored sanding reserves are preserved when the station is broken and replaced.\n* Requires a **Flint Axe** to recover intact.\n* New processing includes:\n\n  * Sanded Wood\n  * Leather\n  * Filed Bone\n  * Woven Wool\n  * Advanced Kiln Glass\n  * Woven Fans\n  * Dye processing\n  * Branch → Twigs\n  * Limestone processing\n  * Recipe Parchment\n  * Rope-related materials\n\nFlower and Ink Sac sanding recipes now provide **improved dye yields** compared to ordinary dye crafting.\n\n---\n\n## Lumber Processing\n\n### Lumber Processor\n\nA new multi-block **Lumber Processor** has been added.\n\nThe structure combines:\n\n* a chopping/work block;\n* a Water Pot;\n* a Crushed Stone finishing block.\n\nIt is used to process stripped logs into more advanced lumber products.\n\nNew lumber materials include:\n\n* **Wooden Boards**\n* **Wooden Beams**\n* **Wooden Sheets**\n* **Wooden Screws**\n\nWashed wood now visually behaves like the chopping section of the processor rather than appearing as a floating partial block.\n\nThe completed Lumber Processor is now recovered using a **Flint Axe**.\n\n### Water Equipment\n\n**Water Bearing Pot**\n\n* Holds half a bucket of water.\n* A full pot is now clearly labeled **Water Bearing Pot (Filled)**.\n\n**Water Pot**\n\n* Used by the Lumber Processor.\n* Also plays a role in later material-processing recipes.\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Woodworking\n\n### Flint File\n\nA new woodworking tool progression has been added:\n\n* Flint Cutter Piece → **Flint File Head**\n* Flint File Head + Stick → **Flint File**\n\nThe Flint File has durability and is used for precision woodworking.\n\n### Wooden Sheets\n\nWooden Beams can now be filed into **Wooden Sheets**.\n\n* Stack size: 64\n\n### Wooden Screws\n\nWooden Boards can now be filed into **Wooden Screws**.\n\n* Stack size: 32\n* Uses a material-overlay texture system designed to support future metal screw variants.\n\n### Wooden Door Hinge\n\n* 8 Wooden Sheets\n* 4 Wooden Screws\n* → **Wooden Door Hinge**\n\nStack size: 8.\n\n### Wattled Daub Door\n\nWattled Daub Doors are now craftable using:\n\n* 16 Wattled Daub Bricks\n* 1 Wooden Door Hinge\n\n---\n\n# Storage & Furniture\n\n## Wooden Chest\n\nThe Wooden Chest has received several fixes and progression changes.\n\n* Proper item name added.\n* Inventory UI corrected.\n* Chest opening/closing animation fixed.\n* No longer remains permanently open after being accessed.\n\n### Wooden Chest Frame\n\nWooden Chests now use a dedicated upgrade component:\n\n* 4 Wooden Sheets\n* 2 Wooden Screws\n* → **Wooden Chest Frame**\n\nThe old Woven Chest + 16 Wooden Boards upgrade requirement has been replaced.\n\n---\n\n## Bookshelf\n\nThe Bookshelf has been heavily reworked.\n\n* UI now follows the cleaner Wooden Grinder-style interface.\n* Installed Books unlock research functionality.\n* Book count now persists when the Bookshelf is broken and replaced.\n* A full Bookshelf holds **4 Books**.\n* Most advanced research recipes require all **4 Books installed**.\n* Multiple valid recipes can now be selected instead of one recipe hiding another.\n* Recipe previews have been restored and corrected.\n* Bookshelf recipe cost is now:\n\n  * 8 Wooden Sheets\n  * 2 Wooden Screws\n\n### Books\n\nBooks can now actually be produced through the intended progression.\n\nA full Bookshelf can also research:\n\n* Book and Quill\n* cooking recipes;\n* advanced food recipes;\n* future recipe unlocks.\n\n---\n\n# Recipe Research System\n\n## Recipe Parchment\n\n**Recipe Parchment** has been introduced as the main recipe-research item.\n\n* Stack size: 1.\n* Blank parchment can be stored in Wooden Cabinets.\n\n..."
		},
